sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant R as SMART React SPA
    participant M as MSAL React / Browser
    participant E as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant G as NGINX / API Gateway
    participant F as SMART FastAPI
    rect rgb(232,241,255)
    U->>B: Open SMART URL
    B->>R: Load React application
    R->>M: Check authenticated account / cached tokens
    alt No authenticated account or usable token
        R->>M: Start sign-in flow
        M->>E: Authorization request: client_id, redirect_uri, scopes, PKCE
        E-->>U: Authenticate / SSO / MFA if required
        U-->>E: Complete authentication
        E-->>B: Redirect to registered redirect URI with authorization code
        B-->>M: Deliver authorization response
        M->>E: Exchange auth code + PKCE verifier for tokens
        E-->>M: Return ID token + access token
        M->>M: Cache account and tokens
    else Authenticated account and valid token exist
        M->>M: Use cached account and token
    end
    M-->>R: Return SMART API access token
    end
    rect rgb(232,247,239)
    U->>R: User action (e.g. Run Scenario)
    R->>G: API request with Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
    G->>F: Forward API request
    F->>F: Validate token / claims and authorize
    F-->>G: API response
    G-->>R: API response
    R-->>B: Render result
    B-->>U: Display SMART response
    end
    Note over R,M: React itself does not authenticate. MSAL orchestrates the OIDC/OAuth flow.
    Note over E: Entra ID authenticates the user and issues tokens.
    Note over G,F: Gateway may validate token; FastAPI still enforces app authorization.